# What a Vercel deployment may contain (docs/deployment/VERCEL_REVIEW_ONLY_DEPLOYMENT.md, docs/deployment/POSTGRESQL.md).
# Allowlist: everything is excluded, then only the application code and the PUBLIC Supabase CA certificate are re-included.
# Folder patterns have no trailing slash: the Vercel CLI tests folder paths without one, so "!/mospi/" would never match.
# The hosted instance reads its review data from Supabase (mospi/db/serving.py), so no data/ file is uploaded at all:
# no raw PLFS folders, stored runs, demo bundle, audit trails, evaluation runs, EDA, notebooks, media, secrets or docs.
/*
!/mospi
!/requirements.txt
!/pyproject.toml
!/vercel.json
!/deploy

# deploy/: only the public CA certificate that verifies the Supabase pooler (sslmode=verify-full); never a key.
/deploy/*
!/deploy/supabase
/deploy/supabase/*
!/deploy/supabase/prod-ca-2021.crt
/*/runs
**/tests
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]

# Never, anywhere (defence in depth; none of these belong in a deployment).
*.parquet
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-*
*.csv
*.zip
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.sav
*.dta
*.log
*.dump
users*.json
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
